      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "text": "Illinois August 2026 ex parte renewal share forecast"
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "The target is Illinois's state row, not a national total or weighted average. Dataset 5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c must be resolved from the August 2026 original (O) submission at first publication. CMS's monthly state tables express ex parte renewals as a percentage of all beneficiaries due for renewal, including those subsequently disenrolled or pending. The numerator is Metric 5a1 and denominator Metric 5. All historical anchors below use the original-period monthly preliminary snapshots, excluding quarterly updated outcomes. Definitions: https://www.medicaid.gov/resources-for-states/downloads/unwinding-data-specifications.pdf"
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Evidence limitation: the official dataset's filtered table, API and CSV could not be retrieved through the web tool. The historical percentages were successfully fetched from official period-specific PDFs, which publish these shares rounded to whole percentage points. Exact ex parte numerator counts and independently recomputed one-decimal historical ratios were not fetched or invented."
      },
      {
        "kind": "tool",
        "tool": "official.lookup",
        "call": "Fetch Illinois's Coverage Retention and Disenrollment Rates by State tables in the official July, August, September, October, November and December 2025 monthly snapshots; exact PDF URLs are listed in sourceContext.",
        "result": "Reporting period: beneficiaries due for renewal; published ex parte percentage. 2025-07: 255612; 65%. 2025-08: 244128; 66%. 2025-09: 221017; 58%. 2025-10: 213528; 65%. 2025-11: 216947; 66%. 2025-12: 222861; 65%. Each table explicitly uses total beneficiaries due for renewal as the denominator."
      },
      {
        "kind": "tool",
        "tool": "official.lookup",
        "call": "Fetch Illinois's original-period state renewal tables in the official January, February and March 2026 monthly snapshots; exact PDF URLs are listed in sourceContext.",
        "result": "2026-01: 163325 beneficiaries due, 63% renewed ex parte. 2026-02: 216487 due, 62% renewed ex parte. 2026-03: 236409 due, 65% renewed ex parte."
      },
      {
        "kind": "tool",
        "tool": "official.lookup",
        "call": "Fetch Illinois's original-period state renewal tables in the official April, May and June 2026 monthly snapshots; exact PDF URLs are listed in sourceContext.",
        "result": "2026-04: 202881 beneficiaries due, 65% renewed ex parte. 2026-05: 206905 due, 66% renewed ex parte. 2026-06: 201287 due, 66% renewed ex parte. June's Illinois row also reports 80% total renewed and 9% pending."
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "The outside-view reference class is the 12 Illinois original-period monthly prints from July 2025 through June 2026. Their base rate is a mean of 64.33% and median of 65%; the latest six average 64.5%. June and the previous August both printed 66%. September's 58% followed by October's 65% demonstrates occasional substantial monthly variation and is retained in the uncertainty sample."
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Level, momentum, one-off and policy effects are separated. The level anchor is June's 66%. Estimated average monthly momentum over the full history is only +0.09 percentage points, so the drift adjustment is zero. No fetched evidence establishes an August-specific one-off adjustment. Illinois HFS dates noncitizen eligibility changes to October 1, 2026, and work requirements and six-month redeterminations to January 1, 2027; therefore the explicit August policy adjustment is zero. HFS describes ongoing work to maximize ex parte verification, but provides no quantified August launch effect. Sources: https://hfs.illinois.gov/info/fedresctr/faqshowwillfedchimpactmedicaid.html and https://hfs.illinois.gov/content/dam/soi/en/web/hfs/about/boardsandcommisions/mac/documents/02262026macpresdeck.pdf"
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Resolution-date verification could not be completed. CMS's fetched official snapshot index lists June 2026 as released September 25, 2026, but supplies no prospective calendar or announcement confirming an August 2026 publication on December 15, 2026. The registered resolutionDate remains 2026-12-15 as required by the ledger contract; it is unverified and has not been inferred from cadence. Source: https://www.medicaid.gov/medicaid-and-chip-eligibility-operations-and-enrollment-snapshot"
      },
      {
        "kind": "math",
        "text": "Prior/update/interval: Use a persistence prior at June's 66.0%, informed by the 12-print Illinois reference class, with momentum, one-off and policy adjustments each zero. The 11 successive changes are [1,-8,7,1,-1,-2,-1,3,0,1,0] percentage points; their sum is 1 and sum of squares is 131. Sample sigma = 3.618136 percentage points, computed as sqrt((131 - 1^2/11)/10). The one-month 80% normal-approximation half-width is 1.28*sigma = 4.631214. For the two-month June-to-August horizon, assuming uncorrelated monthly innovations, multiply by sqrt(2): half-width = 6.549526. Thus 66.0 +/- 6.549526 gives 59.450474 to 72.549526, rounded to final bounds 59.5% and 72.5%. Dispersion is estimated from the fetched whole-percent shares, so tenth-point historical precision is unavailable."
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Upside risk: improved automated matching or an unusually easy-to-verify renewal cohort could raise the share. Downside risk: a matching outage, implementation disruption or harder-to-verify cohort could lower it. A major verification expansion producing a share above 72.5%, or a disruption producing a share below 59.5%, would land outside the interval. These are hypothetical falsification scenarios, not observed August outcomes."
      },
